                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_569">Warwick, Warwickshire. Dominican
                        convent</orgName><p>These fragments are from a choirbook that concords
                        with music in the Old Hall Manuscript, where they are placed next to an
                        Agnus dei ascribed to Robert Chirbury (d. 1454), dean of St Mary's. The book
                        from which these fragments were taken, a copy of Caxton's Sarum Legenda of
                        1488 (BL IB.40010), has a certain post-medieval provenance for Warwick. The
                        choirbook may therefore be identifiable in the inventory of 1465
                        (SC319.16).</p></provenance>
